{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "זכור", :translit "z'chor", :gloss "remember"} {:he "זכור היאך עשה אותך, ויכוננך, בבטן מטיפה סרוחה", :translit "z'chor eikh asah ot'kha, viy'chonenkha, b'veten matipah s'rukhah", :gloss "remember how He made you and established you in the womb from a putrid drop"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "reads 'remember' as recalling God's formation of man in the womb from a putrid drop"}], :frame {:text "The tradition that God forms man in the womb from a putrid drop (טיפה סרוחה) appears in Niddah 31a. Avot 3:1 states that a person should consider his origins, from a putrid drop (מטיפה סרוחה).", :sources ["Niddah 31a" "Avot 3:1"]}} {:quotes [{:he "שאל אביך ויגדך זקניך", :translit "sh'al avikha viyagedkha z'keinekha", :gloss "ask your father and he will tell you, your elders"} {:he "הרי ג' רורות", :translit "harei gish rotrot", :gloss "here are three authorities"} {:he "וסמיך ליה", :translit "u's'mikh lei", :gloss "and it is adjacent to it"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "identifies three authorities: father, elder, and (by adjacency) the prophet of next verse"}], :frame {:text "The verse names two authorities — father and elders — who transmit the national memory. Ba'al HaTurim counts three by reading the adjacent clause 'and they will tell you' (Deuteronomy 32:7) as introducing a third authority, the prophet of the following verse.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 32:7"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "reads 'remember' as recalling God's formation of man in the womb from a putrid drop", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "identifies three authorities: father, elder, and (by adjacency) the prophet of next verse", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:40:49.530183463Z", :model "glm-5.2"}